```python
def is_Monotonic(arr):
    if len(arr) <= 1:
        return True

    increasing = decreasing = True
    for i in range(1, len(arr)):
        if arr[i] < arr[i-1]:
            increasing = False
        elif arr[i] > arr[i-1]:
            decreasing = False

    return increasing or decreasing
```

This function checks if the array is monotonic by iterating through each element and comparing it to the previous element. If the array is not strictly increasing or not strictly decreasing, then it is not monotonic. If it is either strictly increasing or strictly decreasing, then it is monotonic.

